WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.830
- Thank you for singing with me.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.570
That was beautiful.
- Thank you for letting me.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.400
- It's actually hard to sing with you.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.840
I was telling the band.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.270
Because you find yourself listening.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.160
And I'm like, "Oh right,
I'm singing harmony."

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.470
Like you totally lose track 'cause you're

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.252
that captivating.
- Thank you.

00:00:15.252 --> 00:00:17.100
Thank you very much.
- Which is very rare.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.000
I just wanna tell you.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:18.900
That's all.
- Thank you very much.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.090
- And that song is so hopeful.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.080
- [Cynthia] Yeah.
- You forget.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.610
I mean, we've heard it since we were kids,

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.080
but it's so hopeful.
- Every time it comes around,

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.750
you're like, "Oh, that's a good concept

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.010
to think of."
- Yeah.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.840
Were you excited to be a part of the movie

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.832
and get to see that?
- [Cynthia] Really,

00:00:31.832 --> 00:00:32.730
really excited.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.160
I was excited because that
particular song is sort

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.650
of one of those soundtracks that you hear

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.120
over and over again
when you're little and--

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.860
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And then to be able

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.410
to be here now as the Blue Fairy

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.560
for generations coming up to see that,

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.973
is really, really special.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:48.973 --> 00:00:51.400
(audience applauding)
And you were just beautiful.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.430
I was just like, "I wanna glow like that.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.977
I wanna arrive at a party
and glow like that."

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:57.773
But you've always been musical, right?

00:00:57.773 --> 00:00:58.710
- Yes, yeah.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:00:59.543
- Like since you were little.

00:00:59.543 --> 00:01:01.440
So you directed your church choir,

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.940
is this right?
- So, for a little bit.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.290
They asked me to come on

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.673
and be the choir director.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.370
The choir director at the time

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:10.230
wasn't able to do it for
like a couple of weeks.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.880
So he left and then they asked

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.450
if I would do that, but I got into trouble

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.839
because I kept sneaking in gospel music.

00:01:17.839 --> 00:01:18.672
- Oh!

00:01:18.672 --> 00:01:21.270
- So they got really mad at me one time

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.530
and just was like, "You
can't do it anymore

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:23.820
because you keep putting
in this kind of music."

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.680
And I was like, 'cause I was --

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.410
For context, it was a Catholic church.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.750
So we really just do like,

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.700
hymns.
- [Kelly] Hymns, yeah.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.740
- And I wanted more.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:35.880
- [Kelly] Yeah, no, that was me.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.810
I grew up Southern Baptist

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.190
and we did hymns, mostly.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.023
Yeah.
- And that's it.

00:01:39.023 --> 00:01:39.856
- And I love a hymn.

00:01:39.856 --> 00:01:40.740
Hymns are beautiful.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.040
But it's like also, the Lord made us have

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:44.873
other joyful noises.

00:01:44.873 --> 00:01:45.706
- [Cynthia] Other joyful noises.

00:01:45.706 --> 00:01:46.539
- [Both] Yes.

00:01:47.599 --> 00:01:50.640
- So I would just put it in the run of--

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.020
- [Kelly] Can I tell you something?

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.720
I snuck Celine Dion.
- [Cynthia] Well done!

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.197
- It was like, I snuck in, I was like,

00:01:56.197 --> 00:01:58.530
"Yes, it's a song about Jesus.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:01.530
And it's a song that
is so powerful to me."

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.570
And I was like, I just love the song.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.580
And in my head, it was spiritual.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.410
The message could have
been like spiritual,

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.730
and I totally snuck it in

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.650
and got in trouble, but I did it.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.120
- Done it. Too late now!
- You know what?

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:12.960
Sorry's fine.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:13.920
You can say, sorry later.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.134
- Exactly, right.

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:16.274
(audience cheers and applause)

00:02:16.274 --> 00:02:18.390
- So we've been talking
about your childhood,

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.190
and I know you grew up
around a lot of women.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:21.480
So how did that impact you?

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.430
- I think I just learned how to sort

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.920
of be me.
- [Kelly] That's wonderful.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.430
- My mom was always sort of very welcoming

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.263
of who I was.

00:02:30.263 --> 00:02:31.260
She knew I was an arty kid.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.790
She let me go and sing.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:36.540
She let me be in like art programs,

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.380
all of that stuff.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.440
And I think I just got to know myself

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.330
really quickly because I was surrounded

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.890
by women most of the time.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:44.970
Went to a girl school as well.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.337
So it's just like--
- [Kelly] What a blessing.

00:02:46.337 --> 00:02:47.550
- That's who I am.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.870
- But I think that's what also

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.730
makes you specifically magical.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:51.563
- [Cynthia] Thank you.

00:02:51.563 --> 00:02:52.396
- Like somebody so confident

00:02:52.396 --> 00:02:53.229
and comfortable in their skin.

00:02:53.229 --> 00:02:55.170
It's so wonderful that you
had that support growing up.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.100
That's so cool.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:56.933
- [Cynthia] Thank you.

00:02:56.933 --> 00:02:57.766
- 'Cause not all artistic--

00:02:57.766 --> 00:02:59.490
Like we, we all didn't
get that like growing up.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.323
- Yeah.

00:03:00.323 --> 00:03:02.280
- So, well you've been open
about identifying as queer.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.113
- Yes.

00:03:03.113 --> 00:03:04.440
- So were you able to
embrace that as a teenager?

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.273
Was that easy?

00:03:05.273 --> 00:03:07.079
- No, because I don't
think I had the language.

00:03:07.079 --> 00:03:07.912
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:03:07.912 --> 00:03:09.780
- To even know what was going on.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:13.680
I think it's come much later to me now,

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.607
and it's wonderful to just be me.

00:03:17.607 --> 00:03:18.440
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.500
- Really, yeah.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.333
- Refreshing.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.211
- [Cynthia] Yes, very much so.

00:03:21.211 --> 00:03:22.044
- Yeah.

00:03:22.044 --> 00:03:24.270
And I think it sort of
made space creatively

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:28.110
to just sort of let go
of whatever I was hiding.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.750
I guess, you know, you don't
realize you're doing that.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.520
Putting so much energy behind it.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.140
And once you take the energy away

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.259
from concealing something
that is so a part of you

00:03:37.259 --> 00:03:42.259
that you you can't hide it,
you can put it elsewhere.

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.123
- Absolutely.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.720
- Make more wonderful things.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.730
- When you say like, you
didn't know the language

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.800
you mean like there just
wasn't a lot around you

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.660
that kind of even, you
didn't even, you knew it

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.984
was happening, but you didn't
know what to say about it.

00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:54.817
- What to say.

00:03:54.817 --> 00:03:56.587
Yeah, I knew something was different.

00:03:56.587 --> 00:03:58.740
Particularly when I talk about that,

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:02.430
I knew something was different,
but I didn't know what,

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.560
like how, what do I call it?

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.457
What do I say about it?

00:04:05.457 --> 00:04:06.290
And now --

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:07.620
- I've never heard someone
describe it like that.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.880
And that's so poignant.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.640
- Yeah, I think sometimes we assume

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.640
that every queer person
knows it from the beginning.

00:04:16.912 --> 00:04:20.473
Most of us do, but we don't
necessarily know the language

00:04:20.473 --> 00:04:23.580
until someone says, "Hey,
this is, these are words

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.020
that you might want to use.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.168
These are expressions that
you might want to use."

00:04:27.168 --> 00:04:28.001
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:30.600
- This here is some space for you.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.520
So you can speak about yourself

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:35.640
without someone else telling you.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.770
- And I think finding your
people, like when you're young.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:38.603
- [Cynthia] Yeah.

00:04:38.603 --> 00:04:39.699
- Like you're people to kind of help you.

00:04:39.699 --> 00:04:40.560
- [Cynthia] Yeah.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:41.460
- Like cultivate and all of us, you know,

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.500
our personalities, our
character, like who we are.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:44.333
- Yeah.

00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:46.320
- Well we talked a little
about running last time.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.153
- [Cynthia] Yes.

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:47.986
- Um, I still don't.

00:04:47.986 --> 00:04:48.819
(laughs)

00:04:48.819 --> 00:04:52.290
- But I'm just letting you hold
it down for the both of us.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.123
- Sure, I can do that.

00:04:53.123 --> 00:04:55.620
- But you're now about to
do the London marathon.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:56.940
So how has training been?

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.279
What's your playlist like?

00:04:58.279 --> 00:05:02.155
- So playlists it varies
depending on the day.

00:05:02.155 --> 00:05:02.988
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:05:02.988 --> 00:05:04.620
- If I'm having, like, if it's tough,

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.110
and it's been tough to get
out of bed to get on the road,

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.820
I tend to ease myself into it.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.220
So I'll listen to like a Yebba Smith

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:15.060
or I'll give myself I don't
know, like an ease PJ Morton.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.370
A really amazing.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.203
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:18.203 --> 00:05:19.530
- But if it's like a good, good day

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:21.750
and I'm like, I'm ready
for this Renaissance.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:22.583
It's just easy.

00:05:22.583 --> 00:05:23.416
- Oh, Beyonce.

00:05:23.416 --> 00:05:24.294
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:24.294 --> 00:05:28.110
(audience cheers and applause)

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:28.943
- So excited.

00:05:28.943 --> 00:05:30.180
I think there's some fans here.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:31.013
- Good.

00:05:31.013 --> 00:05:31.846
- [Cynthia] There she goes.

00:05:31.846 --> 00:05:33.810
- [Kelly] That's awesome though
that people don't realize--

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.210
That's also, that was gonna
be the cover of my next album.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.043
- Fabulous.

00:05:37.043 --> 00:05:39.306
- And then I was like, "Fine, Beyonce.

00:05:39.306 --> 00:05:41.520
You take the glass horse."

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.315
I, it would look different.

00:05:43.315 --> 00:05:45.060
No, but I, I love her though,

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.470
because I do feel like she has,

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.701
there's certain artists that
I go to when I do work out.

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:49.534
- [Cynthia] Yeah.

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:51.631
- And I, it's like, I
have to be like pumped up.

00:05:51.631 --> 00:05:52.464
- [Cynthia] Yeah.

00:05:52.464 --> 00:05:53.297
- I need them to like amp me up.

00:05:53.297 --> 00:05:54.130
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:54.963
- That's awesome that you have that.

00:05:54.963 --> 00:05:55.796
- That's what she does with me.

00:05:55.796 --> 00:05:56.629
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:56.629 --> 00:05:57.840
- And I'm and the training's
going really well.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:00.870
We're sort of, I think we're
four weeks out of it now.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:01.800
- [Kelly] Do you start getting nervous

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.400
that you have to follow through?

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:06.037
- I had a moment last
week where I was like,

00:06:06.037 --> 00:06:09.180
"Ooh, I do actually have to do this now."

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.650
But I'm really excited.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.180
I'm very, very excited about it.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.704
- Are you convincing yourself right now?

00:06:13.704 --> 00:06:15.725
(laughs)

00:06:15.725 --> 00:06:16.558
- Maybe.

00:06:16.558 --> 00:06:17.391
- I'm very excited about it.

00:06:17.391 --> 00:06:18.690
- Well, I've done the marathon before

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.090
and I think for it sounds terrible,

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.490
but I'm always like, I
know what the end goal is

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.130
and I know how, what it
feels like at the very end.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:28.140
And there's just such a wonderful sense

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.133
of achievement when you manage to get

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:33.083
to the end of that run which
is 26.2 miles by the way.

00:06:33.083 --> 00:06:36.524
- I would feel like Superwoman.

00:06:36.524 --> 00:06:37.623
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:37.623 --> 00:06:39.160
There is that, there is.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.584
There's like a real rush of adrenaline.

00:06:40.584 --> 00:06:42.019
- 'Cause that's what I do in a car.

00:06:42.019 --> 00:06:42.893
- [Cynthia] Right.

00:06:42.893 --> 00:06:44.850
- I'm like, yeah.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:45.900
It's just like 20 miles away.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:46.800
We're just gonna drive there real quick.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:47.633
- [Cynthia] Right.

00:06:47.633 --> 00:06:48.466
- That's crazy.

00:06:48.466 --> 00:06:49.311
- [Cynthia] Yeah.

00:06:49.311 --> 00:06:50.144
- But it is awesome.

00:06:50.144 --> 00:06:50.977
I love people like you, people like Kyle,

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.830
my bass player, he's crazy into marathons.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.350
And it's amazing though that
y'all are holding it down

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.030
for humanity to know what we could do.

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:57.863
- [Cynthia] Right.

00:06:57.863 --> 00:06:58.696
- Like I don't need to
do it because you know.

00:06:58.696 --> 00:07:00.780
We now know we're capable of this.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:01.613
- [Cynthia] Right.

00:07:01.613 --> 00:07:02.446
- Like, yeah.

00:07:02.446 --> 00:07:03.387
So thank you for doing that for us.

00:07:03.387 --> 00:07:04.650
- I appreciate that.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:05.503
Thank you very much.

00:07:05.503 --> 00:07:08.424
- I love, I love that high you
must get at the end though.

00:07:08.424 --> 00:07:09.257
- [Cynthia] Yeah, yeah.

00:07:09.257 --> 00:07:10.125
- It must be so gratifying.

00:07:10.125 --> 00:07:12.210
To complete something so big.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:13.530
- And like it can be anything

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.532
from like three miles to 20 miles.

00:07:15.532 --> 00:07:17.130
The high that you get at the end

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.690
is really like, oh, I did this.

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:19.523
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:19.523 --> 00:07:20.545
- This thing that I wasn't sure I could do

00:07:20.545 --> 00:07:24.930
like two miles ago, I've
managed to finish now.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.640
Like it feels great.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:27.473
Yeah.

00:07:27.473 --> 00:07:28.950
- Yeah, so before you go

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:30.540
I have to ask something
about British people

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:35.540
because I just wanna know
chocolate covered gummy bears.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:38.211
Is this like a thing that
British people just say,

00:07:38.211 --> 00:07:39.044
you know what?

00:07:39.044 --> 00:07:39.877
Just let's watch.

00:07:39.877 --> 00:07:40.710
Just let's watch this first.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:41.550
- [Cynthia] Okay.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:43.608
- Is it like a normal gummy
bear or I'll find out.

00:07:43.608 --> 00:07:44.441
- [Kelly] It's awesome.

00:07:44.441 --> 00:07:45.274
It's awesome.

00:07:45.274 --> 00:07:46.200
I don't know.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.109
Depending on what flavor you would get.

00:07:48.109 --> 00:07:49.253
You're not into it?

00:07:49.253 --> 00:07:50.820
- I don't know, Kelly.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:51.653
- [Kelly] Fine.

00:07:51.653 --> 00:07:52.618
Gimme the bowl.

00:07:52.618 --> 00:07:53.451
- I'm sorry.

00:07:53.451 --> 00:07:54.284
- [Kelly] Give the bowl.

00:07:54.284 --> 00:07:55.117
- It's, I think it's a textural thing.

00:07:55.117 --> 00:07:55.950
- What?

00:07:56.866 --> 00:07:57.810
Is, like, okay.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:01.320
Is the distaste for
chocolate covered gummy bears

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.880
a British thing or a Radcliffe thing?

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:03.990
You ever had one?

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:06.151
- I have had one before.

00:08:06.151 --> 00:08:08.703
I don't like them.

